As a nerd who’s read too much @doughofstadter, I’m excited to share USVC’s investment in @Recursive_SI. @jeffclune and his team aim to scale ideas like his Darwin Gödel Machine to build self-improving AI.

@usvc_ states that the history of AI has been shaped by constraints, initially data, then compute, and now the pace of research itself. The startup USVC is investing in is focused on making AI that can improve itself over time, addressing the next major bottleneck in AI development.

The linked paper introduces the Darwin Gödel Machine, an agent capable of open-ended evolution and self-improvement, which aligns with the goal of creating AI systems that can evolve and enhance their own capabilities.

